{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Getting It Right"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "I Have My Doubts"}, {"type": "position", "content": 2}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 18}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe detailed facts about events or actions in work and social contexts, in written or spoken situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le18ob02re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " The Wh-Clause as Object"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can make wh-clauses after certain verbs with wh-words like <span class=\"italic\">who, whom, whose, what, when, where, why, that</span> and <span class=\"italic\"> how. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use some verbs without an object. <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>I searched online and <span class=\"underline\">found out</span> <span class=\"strong\">why</span> the sky is blue. <li>I <span class=\"underline\">wonder</span> <span class=\"strong\">what</span> happened to Maria since she never called me back.</li></ul></span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "However, there are some verbs for which you need to follow the wh-clause with an object. "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":1,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">remind</span><br/> <div class=\\\"center_text\\\">inform</span><br/> <div class=\\\"center_text\\\">teach</span><br/> <div class=\\\"center_text\\\">warn</span><br/> <div class=\\\"center_text\\\">tell</span><br/> <div class=\\\"center_text\\\">advice</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can also use these verbs with the infinitive after the wh-clause. <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>The doctor <span class=\"underline\">advised</span> his patient <span class=\"strong\">how</span> to take care of his broken leg. <li>The president <span class=\"underline\">reminded</span> citizens <span class=\"strong\">when</span> to stay indoors during the curfew.</li></ul></span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can usually use <span class=\"strong\">ask</span> and <span class=\"strong\">show</span> followed by an object before the wh-clause, but not always. <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>Marcos <span class=\"underline\">asked</span> his mother <span class=\"strong\">how</span> to bake a cake.<li> Marcos <span class=\"underline\">asked</span> (his mother) <span class=\"strong\">how</span> he could bake a cake.</li></ul></span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "If you want to talk about how to do something or get somewhere, the means by which you do these things, you can use <span class=\"strong\">the way</span> instead of <span class=\"strong\">how</span>. <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>I know <span class=\"strong\">how</span> to make money easily. \u2194 I know <span class=\"strong\">the way</span> to make money easily. <li>Could you tell me <span class=\"strong\">how</span> to exit the parking lot? \u2194 Could you tell me <span class=\"strong\">the way</span> to exit the parking lot?</li></ul></span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I understand why this seems hard to believe. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I wonder where she is."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Past Continuous for Frequent Habitual Action"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use the past continuous verb tense to talk about actions that frequently happened in the past. It can also be used to express annoyance with repeated actions in the past. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the past continuous tense (<span class=\"italic\">be + verb-ing</span>) to talk about actions that were in progress at a particular moment or time in the past.<br/> Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>I <span class=\"strong\">was talking</span> with my mother when the phone rang. (longer action happening that was interrupted)<br/> <li>I <span class=\"strong\">was studying</span> while my roommate <span class=\"strong\">was taking</span> a shower. (simultaneous actions)</li></ul></span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "If you want to show that a repeated action in the past annoyed or irritated you, you need to use the past continuous with \u201c<span class=\"strong\">always</span>\u201d or \u201c<span class=\"strong\">constantly</span>\u201d. <br/> Example: <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>Jose <span class=\"strong\">was always talking</span> in class. I could never hear what the teacher was saying. <li>My roommate <span class=\"strong\">was always losing</span> her keys. I hated it when she would have to borrow my keys or call me to come home and open the door.</li></ul></span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "In speaking, you can place more stress on  <span class=\"strong\">always</span> or<span class=\"strong\"> constantly</span> to better show this annoyance."}, {"type": "text", "content": "\u272d\u272d\u272d Using the past continuous in this way does not mean that the actions always happened in the literal sense. It insinuates that they happened very frequently; it was enough to annoy you. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "If you want to say that the actions happened every single time, then you use the <span class=\"italic\">past simple</span>.<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Jose always talked in class. </span>(Jose talked in every class.)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "At social events, I was always waiting in the corner, hoping no one would come my way. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I was always trying to avoid jobs that required dealing with the public. "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "breezy"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "wordy; lots of talking"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Here at Toastmasters, we support breezy introductions."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le18ob02aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use when you tell a story about how things happened."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "master of ceremonies"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the person who runs a formal event"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: My name is Howard Taylor and it is my pleasure to act as master of ceremonies tonight."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le18ob02aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "ways of the past "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the things a person used to do"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We all have our doubts about our ability to change our ways of the past. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le18ob02aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pure fluke"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a great accident; without any planning"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Joining the Toastmasters was a pure fluke."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le18ob02aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "accident of history"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something that was not supposed to happen"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The truth of the matter is that joining Toastmasters was an accident of history. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le18ob02aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "toaster"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a small electrical device used to heat bread (or other foods) until it turns brown"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: My sister-in-law's toaster broke down, and I was doing an internet search for a new one."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le18ob02aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "never look back "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "keeping going in the same direction without having any regrets"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  So I took the plunge, and I have never looked back since."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le18ob02aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "for Pete's sake"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "this is crazy"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I said to myself: I'm fed up with being shy! For Pete's sake! "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le18ob02aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "I can't bear it any longer"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "this is unbearable; things have to change"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I said to myself: I can't bear it any longer! "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le18ob02aud09"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I ask questions about things that happened by accident."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I discuss how things changed because of accidents."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a paragraph talking about changes."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ask 5 - 8  people to name something they did by accident."}, {"type": "text", "content": "With each person, discuss how this event changed things."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Discuss famous inventions and discoveries that were done by accident."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a short paragraph describing 2 -3 of the most interesting stories."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Proofread your paragraph for correct spelling and punctuation."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn10le18ob02re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le18ob02re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn10le18ob02re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "Ladies and gentlemen! Fellow toastmasters! It is my pleasure to call this meeting to order. Welcome one and all! My name is Howard Taylor and it is my pleasure to act as master of ceremonies tonight. Here at Toastmasters, we support breezy introductions, so if you don't mind, I'm going to tell you a little story about how I started in this club.\n<br/>\nI was once a very shy man, if you can believe it. I understand why this seems hard to believe. At social events, I was always waiting in the corner, hoping no one would come my way.  My wife was always asking to go out, but I only wanted to stay at home. I was always trying to avoid jobs that required dealing with the public.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn10le18ob02re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "The truth of the matter is that joining Toastmasters was an accident of history. It was a pure fluke. My sister-in-law, who later joined the club -- I wonder where she is -- ah, there. Please stand for applause, Gertrude.", "id": 2, "time": "62000", "image": "engenn10le18ob02re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "I know you are all wondering where this story is going. As I was saying, my sister-in-law's toaster broke down, and I was doing an internet search for new one, when I came across the website of our own Toastmaster's Club! I wondered how the idea of practicing my public speaking techniques could help draw me out of my shyness.  I had my doubts at first. I feel we all have our doubts about our ability to change our ways of the past.  I said to myself: I'm fed up with being shy! For Pete's sake! I can't bear it any longer! So I took the plunge, and I have never looked back since.", "id": 3, "time": "83500", "image": "engenn10le18ob02re2img03.jpg"}]}}]}], "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can express beliefs, opinions, and annoyance."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can report details, reasons, or results of events or actions. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about past habits.  "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What is something you have done completely by accident?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What happened as a result?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " How is your life different now?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}]}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": " Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "It was a pure fluke!"}], "template_override": 1}, {"questions": [{"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}], "id": 0, "responses": [{"correct": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "id": 0}, {"correct": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "id": 1}]}], "stimuli_ids": [1], "id": 1, "type": "STI", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " \nWelcome to Toastmasters! I will be your master of ceremonies and will guide you through an evening of fun, facts and <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">frivolity</span>.\n"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Content"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback":